  "remediation": {
    "what_changed": "engine f-v1-engine-1.0.1 -> 1.0.2, one accounting-guard fix only (60_strategy_f_run.py::open_position)",
    "u1_diagnosis_was_wrong": "byte-identity of all 10 grids between u1 and u2 proved the 1.0.1 fix (re-check the exhaustion guard after the opposite-crossing flatten) fired zero times out of 86,400 cells",
    "root_cause": "min_entry_equity is recorded INSIDE open_position AFTER the entry's own taker fee is charged, while the pre-entry guard tested equity BEFORE that fee, so an episode decided at a positive-but-sub-fee equity (e.g. +0.33 USDT) posts -4.67 and the registered gate min_entry_equity > 0 fails",
    "fingerprint": "the per-grid minima are always just inside -1x the entry's fee quantum on a 10,000 USDT notional: 1x 5 bps = 5 for the 5 bps grids (full -4.985), 2x = 10 for fee_2x (-9.987), 8x = 40 for cost_attrition_40bps (-39.995)",
    "fix": "open_position refuses the tranche when START_EQUITY + (realized - entry_fee) <= 0 (spelled exactly like the recorded min_entry_equity expression, so the recorded value IS the value that passed the guard), counts entry_refused_exhausted, and the episode loop halts flat on a refusal",
    "red_proof": "the new regression test_entry_the_account_cannot_fund_is_not_opened runs against the frozen 1.0.1 bytes -> FAIL (-360.375 not greater than 0.0), full suite 28 ran / 27 ok / 1 FAIL; against 1.0.2 -> 28/28 OK in the qlib-run container; repo suite unittest discover -s runtime/tests -t runtime/tests -> 342/342 OK",
    "bounded_diff": {
      "prediction": "the fix can only change cells in which u2 had an entry whose own taker fee exhausted the book: per grid, the differing rows must be exactly the u2 rows with min_entry_equity <= 0, each now > 0 with its net_pnl sign unchanged",
      "method": "sha256 per grid + row-level comparison keyed on (symbol, timeframe, window_kind, case_name, brick_pct, rsi_period, spacing_pct, size_multiplier, breakeven_tp_pct, invalidation_pct)",
      "result": "PASS, exactly as predicted: 7,028 differing rows across the 10 grids = 7,028 u2 defect rows (400/91/452/1101/396/540/419/360/403/2866), 0 rows differing outside that set, 0 defect rows unchanged, 0 rows with min_entry_equity <= 0 left in u3, 0 net-PnL sign flips; 79,372 of 86,400 rows byte-identical",
      "entry_refused_exhausted_counter": "sums to 7,028 = the number of refused entries, one per defect cell",
      "no_measurement_field_differed_outside_the_defect_set": true
    }
  },
